{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwy6ghBzpHfLVaPjVXc4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, not any more. Since agents 0.20.0, `MCPClientConnection` starts by sending a `server/discover` probe to check for a stateless MCP server. It only falls back to the old `initialize` handshake, on the same connection, when the server needs it: Legacy Streamable HTTP, SSE and RPC servers. Older code still works and you won't see an error. The difference is that stateless servers never get an `initialize` call.\n\nI checked this against the installed agents 0.27.0 docs (`node_modules/agents/docs/mcp-client.md:191`), which describe the same behaviour. I only found it in the docs; the `server/discover` string didn't turn up in the package's other files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":30913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cd48a39-626a-4612-baf9-7519507c9ab4","uuid":"d7cbe4e2-3570-41a4-9f8b-13ee3eb1a101","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:43:13.632Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwy6gRozUzYdszdAnswt"}
